  "body": "Refs #1448. Part of #1448.\n\nDepends on #3324 (the shared mechanism). Do not start before #3324 is merged. The `blocked` label goes when #3324 is closed.\n\n## What happens\n\nThe 3D kinds select their entry and their first pass alone. The user cannot set where the tool enters or where it leaves. Pocket3D has `links` and refuses a pick (`sane.rs:71-87`). Finish3D and Deburr have no `links`.\n\n## Expected\n\n| Kind | Start | Exit | Seam |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Pocket3D | the descent place of the first pass of each level | the end of the last pass | `machining3d/descent_place.rs:30` (`along_pass`), `:114` (`plunge_at`), `:67-77` (helix); `level_ctx.rs` |\n| Finish3D | the first raster or pattern pass nearest the pick, and its start side | the end of the last pass | `finishing3d/raster.rs`, `finishing3d/polar.rs`; `entry_ramp` (`params.rs:618`) |\n| Deburr | the start of the edge chain nearest the pick | the chain end, or the projection | `finishing3d/deburr.rs` |\n\nA pick on a 3D kind is a model point with Z (question 1 of #3324).\n\n## Why effort:max\n\nThe 3D level planning and the pass order are toolpath algorithms. A user start changes them, and the gouge proof must hold on a surface.\n\n## Laws a pick must keep (refused by name, never moved)\n\n- The descent at the pick does not gouge the part. The entry ramp fits.\n- The first traverse (`operation/first_traverse.rs:45`).\n- The gap link and the verify checks judge the new order.\n\n## Done means\n\n- For each kind: a pin test shows the entry at the pick, a pin test shows the exit, and a pin test shows an impossible pick refused by name.\n- Undo and redo restore the previous path. MCP `edit_operation` sets the picks.\n- Every shipped 3D golden without a pick is byte-identical.\n- Work it in slices, one kind for each PR.\n\nSafety floor: this changes toolpaths and posted G-code.\n",
